<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gutuater</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 51 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gutuater was a leader of the Carnutes in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>, held responsible by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> for the massacre of Roman merchants at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orleans">Cenabum</a> in 52 BCE, which began the great revolt of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vercingetorix">Vercingetorix</a>. After the revolt failed, he was handed over to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a>, who had him executed in 51 BCE. His name may in fact be a Gallic priestly title.</p></div>
